        "title": "My Greatest Accomplishment",
        "excerpt":"Background and inspiration   I started producing around 2015 in Ableton, after taking a keen interest in expressing myself through music. A close friend — a certified genius — could riff his emotions on the piano effortlessly, and I was fascinated by it. Then I stumbled onto deadmau5’s streams, where he was producing live, and I was hooked.   By 2017 I had settled into my dorm at the University of Michigan, but I was missing a space where my expression felt at home. Turns out engineering campus has a few studios. I took the effort to get all the certifications required to use the rooms, and started renting hours.   Process   I never found my “workflow,” but I was obsessed with the pursuit of one — a black hole of never feeling qualified enough for authentic exploration.   Then one day, after a long one, I stopped trying to do it, and in frustration just began to riff.   I liked using sequencers. I liked my synth. I had small chains of workflow that made nice sounds reliably. So — why not plug this here, and this into that, and how about I just fuckin—   And bam.   Out of a chaotic mess layered from chaotic pieces, I found a emergent and pleasant sounding order - and it was representative of exactly what I had just discovered… completely self-referentially.   Result   An intro to a song. Disorganized noises, each with its own inspired idea, rushing together toward the angst, arriving at an order discovered by simply moving forward.   I titled the file on my machine my greatest accomplishment.     Where my head’s at now   I think it represents structured beauty emerging — or showing itself — out of the entropy.   The universe has a law to resolve itself, at least it seems that way. It is a gift to be part of its dance, and it may just be physically impossible not to be.  ","categories": ["Music"],
        "tags": ["music production","ableton","synthesis","emergence"],
