        "title": "Light Commands: A Fly on the Wall",
        "excerpt":"Background and inspiration   Light Commands is the discovery that you can inject voice commands into a smart speaker or phone by pointing a modulated laser at its microphone — no sound, no proximity, no code on the device. The MEMS microphone responds to light as though it were sound.   I dare not take anything away from the massive efforts of Dr. Benjamin Cyr and Dr. Sara Rampazzi on this project. I was honored to be a fly on the wall throughout the process.   Process   My contribution here was presence and a camera. All of the photographs on the project’s website were taken by me.   What I witnessed was science and beautiful raw human effort, ingenuity, and dedication.   Result   lightcommands.com   Where my head’s at now   TODO  ","categories": ["Science"],
